comments.body:
@rjpower I just noticed that this issue fell through the cracks - is this still TODO? e.g. we're _not_:
1. Killing our fork of Harbor any time soon 
2. Planning on really deep changes that'd make keeping up with upstream impractical / irrelevant

> I wonder if a low priority job with 1000 tasks option would be reasonable instead? Maybe we could have a constraint setup so each task has to place to a different worker/pod id.

@rjpower that was my initial thought, but it felt hacky. We would need to add a constraint or abstract resource(s) (à la ray). Multiple-sub-controllers is a good point, deamon construct would expand the contract space, that said if we have a "per worker constraint", there must be a worker construct in the first place. I also thought that it would put more pressure on the endpoints and pollute the job space, which we could ofc workaround, but it felt like a rabbit hole of hacks?

That said - I suspect you have thought about those, and would still prefer to lean on low priority job.
